# {{SUBJECT}} — Obsidian Wiki

This is a personal, LLM-maintained wiki focused on **{{SUBJECT}}**, built as an Obsidian vault. It is meant to grow over time as sources are ingested and questions are asked.

## How it works

- **`sources/`** — raw inputs go here, untouched. Articles, PDFs, transcripts, notes, dumps. Treat as read-only.
- **`pages/`** — the wiki itself. Markdown pages interlinked with Obsidian `[[wikilinks]]`. This is what an LLM maintains.
- **`meta/SCHEMA.md`** — the operating rules. How pages are shaped, how ingest/query/lint work, what conventions to follow. Read this before letting an LLM modify the wiki.
- **`index.md`** — catalog of every page, organized by category. Updated on every ingest.
- **`log.md`** — append-only changelog. Every ingest, edit, or lint pass adds an entry.

## Opening in Obsidian

This folder is the Obsidian vault root (or, if linked into an existing vault, a folder inside one).

- **Standalone vault**: open Obsidian → File → Open vault → choose this folder.
- **Inside an existing vault**: the folder already shows up in the existing vault's file tree — no extra action needed.

Either way, Obsidian's wikilinks, backlinks pane, unresolved-link indicators, and graph view are the way the wiki is navigated and kept honest.

## Working with an LLM

Point the LLM at this folder and tell it to read `meta/SCHEMA.md` first. The schema is the configuration — it defines how the LLM should ingest sources, answer queries, and lint the wiki for problems.

